From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer: C2Buffer: non-DMA-heap linear allocations use their own map

Only the two linear map methods in media/codec2/vndk/C2Buffer.cpp. The newer DMA-heap path assumes every
non-ION allocation is a C2DmaBufAllocation and rejects the existing C2AllocatorBlob gralloc handle.
Non-DMA-heap handles now use the allocation's virtual map, as the ION path already does; genuine DMA-heap
buffers keep the custom map function path. Verified with real C2 BLOB write/read and decoded flexible-YUV
output on the VM. Formerly scripts/patch-codec2.sh.
Against frameworks/av 937eb9047ec2 (REVISION). Apply: patches/apply aosp <LineageOS tree>.
---
diff --git a/media/codec2/vndk/C2Buffer.cpp b/media/codec2/vndk/C2Buffer.cpp
index b22119ffc5..87defedff3 100644
--- a/media/codec2/vndk/C2Buffer.cpp
+++ b/media/codec2/vndk/C2Buffer.cpp
@@ -1253,7 +1253,9 @@ C2Acquirable<C2ReadView> _C2Block1DImpl::mapReadView(
     void *base = nullptr;
     c2_status_t error = C2_OK;
     C2MemoryUsage usage{C2MemoryUsage::CPU_READ, 0};
-    if (android::C2HandleIon::IsUsed()) {
+    // apklayer patch: BLOB and other linear allocators own their mapping.
+    if (android::C2HandleIon::IsUsed() ||
+            !android::C2DmaBufAllocator::CheckHandle(mAllocation->handle())) {
         error = mAllocation->map(
                 offset, len, usage, nullptr, &base);
     } else {
@@ -1282,7 +1284,9 @@ C2Acquirable<C2WriteView> _C2Block1DImpl::mapWriteView(
     void *base = nullptr;
     c2_status_t error = C2_OK;
     C2MemoryUsage usage{C2MemoryUsage::CPU_READ, C2MemoryUsage::CPU_WRITE};
-    if (android::C2HandleIon::IsUsed()) {
+    // apklayer patch: BLOB and other linear allocators own their mapping.
+    if (android::C2HandleIon::IsUsed() ||
+            !android::C2DmaBufAllocator::CheckHandle(mAllocation->handle())) {
         error = mAllocation->map(
                 offset, len, usage, nullptr, &base);
     } else {
